# CODE OWNERS for the repository's security gates and their configuration.
#
# Only ONE account has write access to this repository today (TaylorService-spec). GitHub never lets an author approve
# their own pull request, so the ruleset on main does NOT enable "Require review from Code Owners": with a single
# maintainer it would make every change to these paths unmergeable. Until a second maintainer with write access exists,
# these lines record ownership and request review; enforcement comes from the REQUIRED STATUS CHECKS on main (which a
# deleted or renamed workflow cannot satisfy) and from the ruleset's no-bypass setting.
# Add the second maintainer here, then enable code-owner review in the ruleset.

# CI workflows, including the required security checks.
/.github/                                              @TaylorService-spec

